{"run_id": "repeat_S2_r1_20261113T071825Z", "arm": "S2", "row_id": "G-084", "flow_bucket": "2_multi_period_calculation", "status": "answered", "http_status": 200, "output": "Step-by-step reasoning:\n1. Identify the \"Revenue from operations\" figures for FY2024 and FY2026 from the provided data.\n   - For FY2024 (Year ended 31st March, 2024), the \"Revenue from operations\" is 25,774.09 crores.\n   - For FY2026 (Year ended 31st March, 2026), the \"Revenue from operations\" is 28,162.59 crores.\n2. Calculate the signed difference between the two figures: 28,162.59 - 25,774.09 = 2,388.50 crores.\n\nFinal answer:\n{\n  \"answer_kind\": \"numeric\",\n  \"answer_value\": 25774.09,\n  \"unit\": \"crore\",\n  \"period\": \"FY2024\",\n  \"basis\": \"consolidated\",\n  \"citations\": [\"document_id=4519ab15e6b23c4488c762f6eeddee917aabcacfeacc0cc919bffbdff87a44e1\"],\n  \"abstain\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"The revenue from operations for FY2024 is explicitly stated in the consolidated financial statements.\"\n}", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 8571, "completion_tokens": 819, "total_tokens": 9390}, "latency_ms": 18546, "context_pages": [["4519ab15e6b23c4488c762f6eeddee917aabcacfeacc0cc919bffbdff87a44e1", 343], ["ac7e314c36eb9a51b806663ac56a49b06009ba3c14f05dc019b30d0694fd6d9b", 353]], "rendered_prompt_hashes": ["02543a45b1f35bdb2dcf3d59bcbe5ab439ba060258abdf3babba61ed1bce61a6", "02543a45b1f35bdb2dcf3d59bcbe5ab439ba060258abdf3babba61ed1bce61a6", "02543a45b1f35bdb2dcf3d59bcbe5ab439ba060258abdf3babba61ed1bce61a6"], "rendered_prompt_hash": "02543a45b1f35bdb2dcf3d59bcbe5ab439ba060258abdf3babba61ed1bce61a6", "prompt_set_hash": "abc60a7fb40cc1a4b6109b37103000abc826d9961867d71cf690233dd5da7228", "model_params_hash": "afec57e6000f365bfd8e1584973673ecf7e6aaaff4237f52e39695d1bfdd6277", "label": "SCORED", "samples": [{"status": "answered", "http_status": 200, "output": "Step-by-step reasoning:\n1. Identify the \"Revenue from operations\" figures for FY2024 and FY2026 from the provided data.\n